# Allow-list build context (#785).
#
# Everything is excluded by default and only what the Dockerfile actually
# COPYs is let back in. This keeps the context small (well under 5 MB for a
# clean checkout) and, more importantly, keeps edits to docs/, .github/,
# monitoring/, scripts/ and the SDKs from invalidating the cargo-chef planner
# layer, which runs `cargo chef prepare` over the copied tree.
#
# Dockerfile COPYs that must stay visible:
#   rust-toolchain.toml, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, crates/, migrations/,
#   explorer/ (package.json, package-lock.json, sources for `npm run build`).
# Also kept: docs/examples/webhooks/test_vector.json, pulled in by
# include_str! in crates/lumenqraph-core/src/crypto.rs (test-only, but the
# file must exist for `cargo build --all-targets` / `cargo test`).
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!crates/
!migrations/
!explorer/
!docs/
!docs/examples/
!docs/examples/webhooks/
!docs/examples/webhooks/test_vector.json

# Never ship secrets or local state, even if a rule above would allow them.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/node_modules
**/target
**/.git
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.cache
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/.pgdata
**/.sqlx
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
